{
  "id": "spring-rest-asynchronous-communication",
  "slug": "asynchronous-communication",
  "title": "Asynchronous Communication",
  "category": "Spring Framework",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "heading": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "definition",
          "heading": "Definition:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Asynchronous programming is a programming paradigm that allows a program to initiate a task and continue executing other operations without waiting for the task to complete."
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 26,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "why-asynchronous-programming-in-web-applications",
      "heading": "Why Asynchronous Programming in Web Applications?",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "In traditional synchronous systems, a user's request (like a form submission) blocks the thread until all operations (e.g., sending emails, DB updates) complete. This causes:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Slow response times",
            "Inefficient resource usage",
            "Poor scalability"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 33,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "asynchronous-programming-solves-these-issues-by",
          "heading": "Asynchronous programming solves these issues by:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Running long tasks in the background",
                "Allowing the main thread to handle new requests",
                "Improving performance and responsiveness"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 18,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "when-to-use-async-in-spring-boot",
          "heading": "When to Use Async in Spring Boot?",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Scenario",
                "Use Async?",
                "Why"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Sending confirmation/mass emails",
                  "✅",
                  "Offload long-running I/O"
                ],
                [
                  "Processing large datasets",
                  "✅",
                  "Avoid UI block"
                ],
                [
                  "Long external API calls",
                  "✅",
                  "Don't block main thread"
                ],
                [
                  "Real-time data reporting",
                  "✅",
                  "Improve concurrency"
                ],
                [
                  "Simple CRUD",
                  "❌",
                  "Overhead not justified"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 39,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "enabling-async-in-spring-boot",
      "heading": "Enabling Async in Spring Boot",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
